WEBVTT

00:08:29.631 --> 00:08:32.952
But somehow, we can insulate ourselves
from this problem.

00:08:32.976 --> 00:08:34.577
It's not our problem.

00:08:34.601 --> 00:08:35.954
It's not our burden.

00:08:35.978 --> 00:08:37.573
It's not our struggle.

00:08:38.472 --> 00:08:40.048
I talk a lot about these issues.

00:08:40.072 --> 00:08:42.089
I talk about race

00:08:42.113 --> 00:08:44.386
and this question
of whether we deserve to kill.

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:45.561
And it's interesting,

00:08:45.585 --> 00:08:48.239
when I teach my students
about African American history,

00:08:48.263 --> 00:08:49.530
I tell them about slavery.

00:08:49.554 --> 00:08:50.895
I tell them about terrorism,

00:08:50.919 --> 00:08:53.163
the era that began
at the end of reconstruction

00:08:53.187 --> 00:08:54.612
that went on to World War II.

00:08:54.636 --> 00:08:56.559
We don't really know very much about it.

00:08:56.583 --> 00:08:58.642
But for African Americans in this country,

00:08:58.666 --> 00:09:00.899
that was an era defined by terror.